Title: Link //chrome/browser/ui/tabs:features into chromium_src
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Not a legacy-Windows or cross-build fix: Electron v44.2.0 does not link as
shipped, on any host.

electron/chromium_src builds a hand-picked set of chrome/ sources into its own
static_library rather than depending on chrome's targets, so each one needs its
dependencies restated there. Upstream Electron deliberately keeps
//chrome/browser/themes out of the build (see Electron's own
chore_remove_reference_to_chrome_browser_themes.patch) and compiles
browser_theme_pack.cc itself. In Chromium 152 that file gained a call to
tabs::IsVerticalTabsFeatureEnabled(), which lives in
//chrome/browser/ui/tabs:features -- a dependency of //chrome/browser/themes,
and of nothing Electron links. Nothing catches it until the final link:

  lld-link: error: undefined symbol: bool __cdecl tabs::IsVerticalTabsFeatureEnabled(void)
  >>> referenced by ../../chrome/browser/themes/browser_theme_pack.cc
  >>>               obj/electron/chromium_src\chrome/browser_theme_pack.obj

The target is two files (features.cc, features.h) and its only dependency,
//chrome/browser/ui:ui_features, is already in Electron's link graph, so this
adds nothing but the symbol. Adding features.cc to chromium_src's own sources
would not work: the obj name comes from the basename alone, and
//chrome/browser/devtools/features.cc already claims features.obj in that
target.

Worth sending upstream.

diff --git a/electron/chromium_src/BUILD.gn b/electron/chromium_src/BUILD.gn
index c3f3a29..f04b0c8 100644
--- a/electron/chromium_src/BUILD.gn
+++ b/electron/chromium_src/BUILD.gn
@@ -212,6 +212,7 @@ static_library("chrome") {
     "//chrome/browser/predictors:resource_prefetch_predictor_proto",
     "//chrome/browser/resource_coordinator:mojo_bindings",
     "//chrome/browser/task_manager/common:impl",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/tabs:features",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/webui/tab_search:mojo_bindings",
     "//chrome/browser/web_applications/mojom:mojom_web_apps_enum",
     "//components/enterprise/buildflags",
